  "description": "World - High Resolution Solar Resource (GHI, DIF, GTI, DNI) GIS Data, (Global Solar Atlas) is a dataset listed in energydata.info, an open data portal for energy in developing countries under the section \"Solar\", published or maintained by World Bank Group. Developed by SOLARGIS and provided by the Global Solar Atlas (GSA), this data resource contains solar resource data for: direct normal irradiation (DNI), global horizontal irradiation (GHI), diffuse horizontal irradiation data (DIF), and global irradiation for optimally tilted surfaces (GTI), all in kWh/m² covering the globe. Data is provided in a geographic spatial reference (EPSG:4326). Coverage: 214 countries. It has 8 files in JSON, ZIP. The portal files it under Solar. The portal gives 2020 as the release date. It is reached through the links recorded on this page, with the catalogue entry as the discovery route. Access is free of charge and open. The licence is CC-BY-4.0. Caveats: this record was written from the catalogue listing only, so the linked page was not opened, its contents and current availability were not checked, and the description may lag the source. It can support power-system and electrification planning studies. Related record: the catalogue-level record data-energydata-info-world-bank.",
